{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"6d33b9e2-77b5-44c8-b174-ec79338e5c4d","title":"Snell's law: light bending at a boundary"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6d33b9e2-77b5-44c8-b174-ec79338e5c4d","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Light changes direction when it crosses between materials. We measure its angle from the normal, perpendicular to the boundary—not from the surface.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Snell's law"},{"op":"figure","id":"boundary","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.8,3.8],"y":[-3.6,3.6],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"surface","from":[-3.6,0],"to":[3.6,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"entry","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"normal","from":[0,-3.3],"to":[0,3.3],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.7,3.2],"text":"normal","size":"small"},{"kind":"text","at":[2.5,2.3],"text":"air: n = 1.00"},{"kind":"text","at":[-2.1,-2.3],"text":"glass: n = 1.50"},{"kind":"segment","id":"incident","from":[-3,3],"to":{"at":"entry"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"entry"},"from":[0,3],"to":[-3,3],"r":0.23,"label":"45°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"law","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6d33b9e2-77b5-44c8-b174-ec79338e5c4d","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Entering glass increases the refractive index. Snell's law therefore gives a smaller sine, and a smaller angle from the normal.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"transmit","on":"boundary","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"refracted","from":{"at":"entry"},"to":[1.603567,-3],"arrow":true,"label":"refracted"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"substitute","anchor":{"el":"law","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\sin\\theta_2=\\frac{1.00}{1.50}\\sin45^\\circ\\approx0.471"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6d33b9e2-77b5-44c8-b174-ec79338e5c4d","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The refracted angle is about twenty-eight degrees: the ray bends toward the normal. In reverse, leaving glass for air bends it away.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"angle_result","on":"boundary","marks":[{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"entry"},"from":[0,-3],"to":{"on":"refracted","t":1},"r":0.26,"label":"28.1°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"substitute","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\theta_2=\\sin^{-1}(0.471)\\approx28.1^\\circ<45^\\circ"},{"op":"text","id":"takeaway","anchor":{"el":"answer","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Higher index → toward the normal"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Going from glass into air, does the ray bend toward or away from the normal?","expected_gist":"Away from the normal, when transmission occurs."}}}
